2026-09-15 | RECON | The REAL problem: web.report_assets_common includes web/static/fonts/fonts.scss (manifest:256->309), which declares the Arabic face at https://fonts.odoocdn.com (fonts.scss:27-36). Served report bundle: 1 occurrence of fonts.odoocdn.com. Served backend bundle: 0. PDFs render server-side, so an unreachable CDN = broken Arabic in generated documents.
2026-09-15 | CORRECTION | "Just declare our @font-face later and it wins" DOES NOT WORK. Measured in Chromium 3x: the browser fetches BOTH sources. The first two attempts were invalid (a 404, then Lato which has no Arabic glyphs); the third used the real Noto Sans Arabic and still fetched both. Odoo's declaration cannot be out-voted — only left unreferenced.
2026-09-15 | IMPLEMENTED | acczed_theme/static/src/scss/_acczed_fonts.scss declares family "acczed Arabic" from self-hosted NotoSansArabic-{Regular,Bold}.ttf, and sets $font-family-sans-serif BEFORE bootstrap_overridden_report.scss (whose value is !default). Wired via ('before', ...) in web.report_assets_common.
